    dict(key='01-poster', kind='poster', title='Insecure Deserialization and Its Defences',
         body=None,
         narration="Hello, and welcome. [[slnc 400]] This video explains insecure deserialization and its defences, in Java. [[slnc 300]] This video is presented by Jayasekhar Konduru. [[slnc 600]] First, a simple definition. [[slnc 300]] Deserialization rebuilds an object from bytes. [[slnc 300]] In Java's built-in format, the bytes name the classes to build, and some classes run code while they are being rebuilt. [[slnc 300]] So whoever writes the bytes chooses what the server builds, and some of what it runs. [[slnc 600]] Think of a flat-pack kit that comes with its own instructions, and you must follow each step while you unpack the box. [[slnc 300]] If a stranger packed the box, a stranger wrote the steps. [[slnc 600]] Our example is an online store that keeps the shopping cart in a cookie."),
