    dict(key='07-costs', kind='bullets', title='What It Costs',
         body=['An allow-list needs upkeep as classes change', 'A filter stops classes, not lies', "Java's serialized form breaks easily", '  when classes change', 'Signing needs a key, and key rotation', 'A cart kept on the server avoids all of it'],
         narration="Nothing is free. [[slnc 400]] Here is what the defences cost. [[slnc 500]] An allow-list of classes needs upkeep: every new field type has to be added. [[slnc 500]] A filter stops unknown classes, but not a lie told with allowed ones, like a forged price. [[slnc 500]] Java's serialized form breaks easily when a class changes, so old cookies stop working. [[slnc 500]] Signing needs a secret key, and a plan to change it. [[slnc 300]] And keeping the cart on the server, with only a session number in the cookie, avoids the whole problem."),
